2
00:00:06,521 --> 00:00:09,896
<i>Look, I didn't want to be
a half-blood.</i>

3
00:00:12,313 --> 00:00:15,938
<i>Being a half-blood is dangerous.
It's scary.</i>

4
00:00:17,271 --> 00:00:22,813
<i>Most of the time it gets you killed,
in painful, nasty ways.</i>

5
00:00:25,438 --> 00:00:29,146
<i>If you think you might be one of us,
my advice is</i>

6
00:00:29,396 --> 00:00:31,063
<i>turn away while you still can,</i>

7
00:00:32,105 --> 00:00:33,563
<i>because once you know what you are...</i>

8
00:00:35,271 --> 00:00:38,605
<i>they'll sense it too
and they'll come for you.</i>

9
00:00:40,730 --> 00:00:42,855
<i>Don't say I didn't warn you.</i>

10
00:00:54,230 --> 00:00:57,355
<i>My name is Percy Jackson.
I'm twelve years old.</i>

11
00:00:58,646 --> 00:01:00,230
<i>Am I a troubled kid?</i>

12
00:01:02,355 --> 00:01:04,146
<i>Yeah, you could say that.</i>

13
00:01:05,271 --> 00:01:08,396
<i>Bad grades, bullies, all the normal stuff.</i>

14
00:01:10,646 --> 00:01:12,480
<i>And then there's some other stuff.</i>

15
00:01:14,063 --> 00:01:16,896
<i>Some stuff
that's... maybe not so normal.</i>

16
00:01:28,021 --> 00:01:32,563
<i>That's me, back in second grade.
Why was I up there?</i>

17
00:01:33,938 --> 00:01:35,146
<i>I saw something.</i>

18
00:01:36,605 --> 00:01:40,563
<i>At least... I could have sworn
I saw something.</i>

19
00:01:44,896 --> 00:01:46,480
<i>When you say
you something like that,</i>

20
00:01:46,480 --> 00:01:48,438
<i>you wind up in this guy's office.</i>

21
00:01:49,063 --> 00:01:52,480
<i>Good news, he's saying
there's nothing to worry about.</i>

22
00:01:53,271 --> 00:01:55,230
<i>It's all in my imagination,</i>

23
00:01:55,896 --> 00:01:58,396
<i>but if it happens again,
make sure to tell someone.</i>

24
00:02:02,230 --> 00:02:03,355
<i>It happened again.</i>

25
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:07,730
<i>These impossible things
that felt like they walked</i>

26
00:02:07,855 --> 00:02:09,896
<i>right out of the stories
my mom always told me.</i>

27
00:02:10,938 --> 00:02:14,563
<i>So real one minute, and then the next...</i>

28
00:02:16,230 --> 00:02:17,521
What a loser.

29
00:02:18,563 --> 00:02:21,605
<i>Hey, fellas, wanna come hear
about the imaginary stuff I see?</i>

30
00:02:22,271 --> 00:02:25,355
<i>It's not a thing
you wanna be saying, to anyone,</i>

31
00:02:25,980 --> 00:02:27,021
<i>so I didn't.</i>

32
00:02:28,396 --> 00:02:31,105
<i>Then... something changed.</i>

33
00:02:34,105 --> 00:02:35,313
<i>I met Grover.</i>

34
00:02:36,230 --> 00:02:37,896
<i>We had a lot in common.</i>

35
00:02:38,021 --> 00:02:39,605
- Only he--

36
00:02:39,730 --> 00:02:40,938
Mm-mm.

37
00:02:43,188 --> 00:02:46,146
<i>And not just because we were both
at the bottom of the food chain.</i>

38
00:02:47,146 --> 00:02:48,230
<i>And you know what?</i>

39
00:02:48,230 --> 00:02:50,771
<i>It felt good to talk about these things
with Grover.</i>

40
00:02:51,063 --> 00:02:53,271
<i>I could almost believe
they were imaginary.</i>

41
00:02:53,896 --> 00:02:56,313
<i>Weird, but harmless.</i>

42
00:02:58,813 --> 00:03:00,563
<i>Until the day that changed, too.</i>

43
00:03:03,771 --> 00:03:06,230
<i>Until the day one of them decided
to come for me.</i>

44
00:03:10,396 --> 00:03:12,605
{\an8}

45
00:03:15,896 --> 00:03:19,771
What you see here,
they are not fictions.

46
00:03:20,855 --> 00:03:23,021
They are not fantasies.

47
00:03:24,105 --> 00:03:30,938
What you see here are the truest
and deepest parts of yourselves.

48
00:03:32,313 --> 00:03:33,313
Friends...

49
00:03:34,521 --> 00:03:35,771
the gods...

50
00:03:36,730 --> 00:03:39,646
the monsters, the heroes

51
00:03:40,063 --> 00:03:41,938
you see here in this room

52
00:03:42,938 --> 00:03:46,646
are reminders of what we are capable of.

53
00:03:47,980 --> 00:03:49,813
Now, on your worksheets,

54
00:03:49,938 --> 00:03:53,855
I want you to choose one of the subjects
you see here

55
00:03:54,396 --> 00:03:56,105
and describe it.

56
00:03:56,813 --> 00:03:58,938
Not just how it looks...

57
00:04:01,146 --> 00:04:02,771
but how it makes you feel.

58
00:04:03,855 --> 00:04:05,605
Hmm? Okay, come on.

59
00:04:15,813 --> 00:04:16,855
<i>What do you see?</i>

60
00:04:21,230 --> 00:04:22,438
<i>Perseus...</i>

61
00:04:24,146 --> 00:04:25,230
that's me.

62
00:04:25,605 --> 00:04:27,980
Mm-hmm,
that's who you're named after.

63
00:04:30,188 --> 00:04:31,813
Is that why you named me after him?

64
00:04:33,230 --> 00:04:34,646
Because he was a hero?

65
00:04:35,271 --> 00:04:37,188
What makes you think he was a hero?

66
00:04:38,730 --> 00:04:40,355
Because he kills monsters.

67
00:04:41,521 --> 00:04:44,063
And what makes you think
that she was a monster?

68
00:04:44,688 --> 00:04:45,688
Mom...

69
00:04:47,355 --> 00:04:50,063
Not everyone
who looks like a hero is a hero,

70
00:04:50,605 --> 00:04:53,771
and not everyone who looks
like a monster is a monster.

71
00:04:54,521 --> 00:04:59,271
I named you after him
because when he was a very little boy,

72
00:04:59,730 --> 00:05:02,271
he and his mother were placed
in a wooden chest

73
00:05:02,396 --> 00:05:06,230
and cast out into the sea
by a very angry king.

74
00:05:06,688 --> 00:05:12,605
Alone, afraid. And at night, his mother
would whisper in his ear,

75
00:05:13,355 --> 00:05:15,688
"Hold fast, Perseus."

76
00:05:16,146 --> 00:05:21,396
"Brave the storm that was made
to break us for we are unbreakable

77
00:05:21,521 --> 00:05:23,271
"as long as we have each other."

78
00:05:24,813 --> 00:05:27,688
And against all odds,

79
00:05:27,688 --> 00:05:31,605
he managed to find his way
to a happy ending.

80
00:05:37,021 --> 00:05:38,396
-  Percy?

81
00:05:38,521 --> 00:05:39,813
- Mom?

82
00:05:40,188 --> 00:05:44,813
- I'm right here, sweetie! Mommy's here!

83
00:05:45,230 --> 00:05:46,438
Mr. Jackson,

84
00:05:47,105 --> 00:05:49,563
you will learn to control yourself,
do you understand me?

85
00:05:49,688 --> 00:05:51,855
- Me?
- Do you understand me?

86
00:05:51,980 --> 00:05:55,688
He can't help it, Mrs. Dodds.
Percy's special.

87
00:05:55,813 --> 00:05:58,188
- That's enough.

88
00:06:01,355 --> 00:06:02,855
Pay them no mind.

89
00:06:05,188 --> 00:06:06,396
When you're ready to hear

90
00:06:06,646 --> 00:06:09,938
what the gods have in store for you,
they'll tell you.

91
00:06:11,146 --> 00:06:12,146
I believe in you.

92
00:06:13,105 --> 00:06:16,313
And I believe you'll be needing this.

93
00:06:16,563 --> 00:06:18,438
-  Hmm?

94
00:06:19,188 --> 00:06:20,271
Hang on to that.

95
00:06:21,063 --> 00:06:22,563
'Tis a mighty instrument.

96
00:06:34,021 --> 00:06:36,855
There are all sorts of schools of thought
about what drives that kind of bullying.

97
00:06:36,980 --> 00:06:39,146
Childhood trauma,
feelings of inadequacy...

98
00:06:39,313 --> 00:06:41,188
Look, I get that Nancy has issues,

99
00:06:41,188 --> 00:06:43,396
I'm just getting tired
of her taking them out on me.

100
00:06:44,188 --> 00:06:47,730
I feel like... maybe it's time
to do something about it.

101
00:06:48,146 --> 00:06:50,063
You could make an appointment
to see Mr. Kane.

102
00:06:50,063 --> 00:06:52,521
- He's really good at talking--
- I was thinking more like shoving Nancy

103
00:06:52,646 --> 00:06:53,771
in the nearest dumpster.

104
00:06:54,896 --> 00:06:55,896
- Oh.

105
00:06:55,896 --> 00:06:59,188
- Oh, no. No, no, no, no, no, no, no.

106
00:06:59,313 --> 00:07:01,313
No, if there's one thing
I know about bullies,

107
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:03,730
it is that you should never,
ever stand up to them.

108
00:07:04,813 --> 00:07:06,146
That doesn't sound right.

109
00:07:07,646 --> 00:07:08,646
Look...

110
00:07:09,355 --> 00:07:11,313
I know this place is hard
for people like us.

111
00:07:11,938 --> 00:07:13,480
But we're not gonna be here forever.

112
00:07:13,938 --> 00:07:15,313
There are better places out there.

113
00:07:16,896 --> 00:07:18,730
-  Oops.

114
00:07:20,855 --> 00:07:21,855
Percy...

115
00:07:23,021 --> 00:07:24,021
-  No, don't!

116
00:07:29,021 --> 00:07:30,688
Percy pushed me!

117
00:07:30,813 --> 00:07:33,021
-  Nancy, are you okay?
-  He just pushed Nancy!

118
00:07:40,521 --> 00:07:43,396
<i>There you are.</i>

119
00:07:44,355 --> 00:07:47,938
<i>We're not fools, Percy Jackson.</i>

120
00:07:48,521 --> 00:07:51,021
Mrs. Dodds, you okay?

121
00:07:51,980 --> 00:07:55,480
<i>It was only a matter of time
before we found you.</i>

122
00:08:03,230 --> 00:08:06,813
<i>Where is it, half-blood?</i>

123
00:08:07,563 --> 00:08:09,688
<i>Where is it?</i>

124
00:08:31,230 --> 00:08:32,938
- Is he okay?
- Is he dead?

125
00:08:35,271 --> 00:08:37,813
-  Give him some room, please.

126
00:08:41,146 --> 00:08:42,313
What happened?

127
00:08:43,813 --> 00:08:45,063
Where's Mrs. Dodds?

128
00:08:45,313 --> 00:08:47,146
I didn't do anything to him!

129
00:08:47,521 --> 00:08:49,605
- He pushed me.
- Everyone, go back to your lunches.

130
00:08:49,938 --> 00:08:52,188
It's all right.
Percy just needs a moment, that's all.

131
00:08:53,521 --> 00:08:56,063
I don't understand.
Didn't anyone just see that?

132
00:08:56,063 --> 00:08:58,480
- Where's Mrs. Dodds?

133
00:09:01,271 --> 00:09:05,021
Percy, there's no one here by that name.

134
00:09:07,563 --> 00:09:11,396
All right, class, let's move along.
Let's go. Finish your lunch.

135
00:09:16,480 --> 00:09:20,646
<i>The truth...
can be so very hard to determine...</i>

136
00:09:22,063 --> 00:09:25,605
but in this case,
the truth seems very hard to deny.

137
00:09:27,480 --> 00:09:28,771
Mr. Jackson,

138
00:09:29,105 --> 00:09:32,313
a number of your classmates saw you
and Mr. Underwood

139
00:09:32,521 --> 00:09:34,355
arguing with Ms. Bobofit,

140
00:09:34,730 --> 00:09:38,730
yet you have offered no explanation
for how she ended up in that fountain,

141
00:09:39,313 --> 00:09:40,646
other than, uh...

142
00:09:43,021 --> 00:09:44,855
"I didn't touch Nancy."

143
00:09:46,771 --> 00:09:51,355
Now, isn't there anything else
you'd like to say for yourself?

144
00:09:53,938 --> 00:09:55,521
I didn't touch Nancy.

145
00:09:57,688 --> 00:09:59,021
Okay.

146
00:10:00,313 --> 00:10:03,605
Mr. Underwood?
Do you have anything to add?

147
00:10:09,021 --> 00:10:10,105
Yes.

148
00:10:11,813 --> 00:10:12,813
I do.

149
00:10:13,188 --> 00:10:15,438
-  Go on.

150
00:10:18,063 --> 00:10:21,646
Percy had told me earlier in the day
that he wanted to get back at Nancy

151
00:10:21,646 --> 00:10:23,646
- for all she'd done to us.
- Grover?

152
00:10:24,105 --> 00:10:26,480
And he isn't being truthful
about what happened at the fountain.

153
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:27,980
- Grover!
-  Excuse me.

154
00:10:28,230 --> 00:10:32,521
Are you saying you saw
Mr. Jackson assault Ms. Bobofit?

155
00:10:40,396 --> 00:10:41,396
Yes,

156
00:10:42,105 --> 00:10:43,105
I did.

157
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:53,896
None of this is easy.

158
00:10:55,813 --> 00:10:56,813
Not for you,

159
00:10:57,605 --> 00:10:58,688
not for any of us.

160
00:10:59,646 --> 00:11:01,521
I'm very concerned about you, Percy.

161
00:11:02,105 --> 00:11:03,855
I saw what happened at the museum.

162
00:11:03,980 --> 00:11:06,021
I didn't touch Nancy.

163
00:11:06,188 --> 00:11:08,063
I know you didn't.

164
00:11:09,938 --> 00:11:13,771
At least, I know you think you didn't.

165
00:11:16,355 --> 00:11:19,271
Do you want to tell me
what you think did happen?

166
00:11:20,063 --> 00:11:23,438
- You can tell me. I might just understand.

167
00:11:23,771 --> 00:11:24,896
You wanna bet?

168
00:11:25,521 --> 00:11:27,313
Percy...

169
00:11:28,730 --> 00:11:32,896
I've seen a lot of young people
go through this sort of thing in my time,

170
00:11:33,980 --> 00:11:36,355
but of all of them, I suspect that...

171
00:11:37,563 --> 00:11:39,896
you might have the most difficult journey.

172
00:11:40,730 --> 00:11:43,980
I suspect you are special.

173
00:11:44,605 --> 00:11:48,646
- So much more so than you know.
- Just... stop.

174
00:11:49,230 --> 00:11:51,938
Okay? I don't need any more stories

175
00:11:52,063 --> 00:11:54,646
- about how special I don't realize I am.

176
00:11:54,980 --> 00:11:56,021
They aren't helping.

177
00:11:56,605 --> 00:11:58,313
- This is my ride. I'm going home.

178
00:12:18,730 --> 00:12:21,188
There's nothing wrong
with the plumbing in this building.

179
00:12:21,563 --> 00:12:22,855
Maybe you should see a doctor.

180
00:12:23,021 --> 00:12:24,563
How do you know
I'm not a doctor, huh?

181
00:12:24,563 --> 00:12:26,438
Have you considered
eating more fruit?

182
00:12:26,563 --> 00:12:30,646
Hey! I eat plenty of fruit.
Have you considered eating more fruit?

183
00:12:33,938 --> 00:12:35,855
Oh! Hello, Percy.

184
00:12:36,688 --> 00:12:38,438
Hey, Eddie, sorry about that.

185
00:12:39,021 --> 00:12:43,188
I'm walking out, you're walking in.
I should be apologizing to you.

186
00:12:54,063 --> 00:12:56,896
-  W-- Hell, hello.

187
00:12:58,105 --> 00:13:00,438
Welcome home, genius.

188
00:13:01,688 --> 00:13:02,896
Is my mom home from work?

189
00:13:02,896 --> 00:13:05,063
Oh, is that all you got to say to me? Huh?

190
00:13:05,688 --> 00:13:08,813
- After failing out of school?
- I didn't fail out of school.

191
00:13:08,938 --> 00:13:11,063
Your principal called,
and that's what he said.

192
00:13:11,230 --> 00:13:12,480
He said you got kicked out.

193
00:13:13,438 --> 00:13:14,771
They called Mom's cell.

194
00:13:15,563 --> 00:13:18,438
- You answer Mom's cell?
- I answer whatever's ringing.

195
00:13:19,896 --> 00:13:21,896
So, what'd you get kicked out for, hmm?

196
00:13:22,688 --> 00:13:24,855
He said I attacked a kid
on a field trip.

197
00:13:27,230 --> 00:13:28,230
Okay.

198
00:13:28,855 --> 00:13:32,105
All right, if... But still,
if you're gonna live under my roof,

199
00:13:32,938 --> 00:13:34,938
- you gotta live by my rules.
-  Your roof?

200
00:13:35,063 --> 00:13:37,896
- My mom is the only one employed here.
- Excuse me?

201
00:13:38,605 --> 00:13:41,605
I have a job. What does it look like
I'm doing right now?

202
00:13:42,146 --> 00:13:44,063
Losing at imaginary poker.

203
00:13:44,438 --> 00:13:46,480
You would think that
because you're a child,

204
00:13:46,605 --> 00:13:49,021
- and you don't understand things like--
-  Where's my mom?

205
00:13:49,230 --> 00:13:50,230
I don't know.

206
00:13:50,355 --> 00:13:52,980
I don't know where your mom is.
I'm not Nostradamus.

207
00:13:53,355 --> 00:13:56,146
What are we doing, Percy? Every time!

208
00:13:57,188 --> 00:13:59,438
Wow! Wow!

209
00:14:07,605 --> 00:14:09,980
<i>♪ But now the current's stronger ♪</i>

210
00:14:10,438 --> 00:14:15,771
<i>♪ No, I couldn't get out if I tried
but you convinced me, baby ♪</i>

211
00:14:15,896 --> 00:14:18,146
<i>♪ It was all in my mind ♪</i>

212
00:14:18,438 --> 00:14:19,771
-  Mom...

213
00:14:22,896 --> 00:14:25,813
I'm really sorry. I tried this time.
You know how hard I've been trying,

214
00:14:25,813 --> 00:14:29,355
but this time, it really wasn't my fault.
It really wasn't my fault.

215
00:14:29,855 --> 00:14:30,938
<i>♪ 'Cause if rain don't pour... ♪</i>

216
00:14:30,938 --> 00:14:32,146
I'm all wet now.

217
00:14:32,688 --> 00:14:35,146
I'm sorry.
I'm just very glad to see you.

218
00:14:35,896 --> 00:14:38,188
I found Gabe on the phone
with the headmaster,

219
00:14:38,355 --> 00:14:40,730
he told me what he thinks happened
with Nancy Bobofit.

220
00:14:41,355 --> 00:14:44,146
I told him I believe my kid.
It was a real short call.

221
00:14:45,896 --> 00:14:48,855
Hey, all that matters
is that you're here, okay?

222
00:14:49,771 --> 00:14:52,396
And that I had enough time...

223
00:14:53,563 --> 00:14:55,355
to pick up your welcome home gift.

224
00:15:04,771 --> 00:15:08,230
Mr. Brunner called me, too.
He told me about Grover.

225
00:15:09,896 --> 00:15:11,063
Do you wanna talk about it?

226
00:15:15,438 --> 00:15:17,938
Is there something else
you wanna talk about?

227
00:15:21,605 --> 00:15:28,230
Something happened to me.
Something has been happening to me.

228
00:15:29,146 --> 00:15:33,396
More than just my mind wandering
and it got worse and...

229
00:15:36,271 --> 00:15:37,355
I'm scared.

230
00:15:41,063 --> 00:15:42,896
- Gabe?
- Mom?

231
00:15:45,105 --> 00:15:47,563
I don't know how anyone expects me

232
00:15:47,688 --> 00:15:50,730
- to get any work done--
- Percy and I are leaving for Montauk.

233
00:15:50,855 --> 00:15:52,521
I'll... I'll have the car back
by Sunday morning.

234
00:15:52,521 --> 00:15:54,813
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
Since when are you going to Montauk?

235
00:15:54,813 --> 00:15:58,271
I called to reserve the place
as soon as I got off the phone with Yancy.

236
00:15:58,688 --> 00:15:59,688
Who's Yancy?

237
00:16:00,605 --> 00:16:01,605
The school.

238
00:16:02,938 --> 00:16:03,938
Okay.

239
00:16:05,146 --> 00:16:10,730
- And why exactly am I okay with this?
- Because on my way home on Sunday,

240
00:16:10,730 --> 00:16:13,521
I'm gonna stop at D'Angelo's
and pick up sandwiches in time for tipoff,

241
00:16:13,688 --> 00:16:16,438
but if you make this miserable,
I'm gonna go anyway

242
00:16:16,438 --> 00:16:19,855
and then I'm gonna eat my sandwich
and yours while I listen to the game

243
00:16:19,855 --> 00:16:21,521
- on the radio.
- You know I hate watching

244
00:16:21,521 --> 00:16:23,063
- the Knicks alone.
- So do I!

245
00:16:23,063 --> 00:16:25,771
W-- Make sure they put the hot peppers
on my sandwich, please?

246
00:16:25,980 --> 00:16:28,480
- Not if you're gonna ask like that.
- I said, "Please."

247
00:16:33,480 --> 00:16:36,105
Please, could you have them

248
00:16:36,355 --> 00:16:38,855
- put the peppers on my sandwich?
- You got it.

249
00:16:42,271 --> 00:16:44,563
Take your shoes off
before you get in my car.

250
00:16:44,730 --> 00:16:45,771
You understand me?

251
00:16:47,896 --> 00:16:50,605
We have a lot to talk about,
but uh, that storm out there,

252
00:16:50,605 --> 00:16:52,813
it's getting angrier,
so let's get ahead of it.

253
00:16:52,813 --> 00:16:56,563
We'll talk at the beach, okay?
Pack your bag. Let's go.

254
00:17:23,438 --> 00:17:26,355
<i>Who are you?</i>

255
00:17:29,063 --> 00:17:33,688
<i>So weak. So scared.</i>

256
00:17:34,063 --> 00:17:36,355
<i>So sad.</i>

257
00:17:37,271 --> 00:17:43,063
<i>Run away, little hero,
before you get hurt.</i>

258
00:17:51,938 --> 00:17:52,938
We're here.

259
00:17:55,146 --> 00:17:56,146
On three?

260
00:17:57,896 --> 00:17:58,896
Ready?

261
00:17:59,521 --> 00:18:03,230
One, two... [laughs] ...three!

262
00:18:33,146 --> 00:18:35,896
I found the good marshmallows.
Ones that don't burn so easy.

263
00:18:37,688 --> 00:18:39,646
I don't think it was ever
the marshmallows' fault

264
00:18:39,646 --> 00:18:41,105
I wasn't paying attention.

265
00:18:54,063 --> 00:18:55,063
Mom...

266
00:18:56,521 --> 00:18:58,188
I need to talk to you about something.

267
00:19:06,188 --> 00:19:10,396
I'm used to feeling weird.
I'm used to the world feeling weird to me.

268
00:19:11,105 --> 00:19:14,063
Like a puzzle with half the wrong pieces.

269
00:19:16,271 --> 00:19:19,855
I try to pay attention. I really try, but...

270
00:19:21,230 --> 00:19:24,271
then I'm daydreaming. I can't help it.

271
00:19:27,355 --> 00:19:28,355
But lately...

272
00:19:29,396 --> 00:19:33,605
it hasn't felt like daydreaming.
It's felt...

273
00:19:34,855 --> 00:19:38,813
I don't know. More real, maybe?

274
00:19:41,980 --> 00:19:43,563
And then we were at the museum and...

275
00:19:45,146 --> 00:19:46,271
You saw something.

276
00:19:50,730 --> 00:19:55,605
Something that felt real to you,
but no one else could see?

277
00:20:08,563 --> 00:20:10,021
What did she say to you?

278
00:20:13,980 --> 00:20:17,688
She? How did you know it was a she?

279
00:20:22,188 --> 00:20:24,605
Do you know why we come
to this cabin every year?

280
00:20:24,813 --> 00:20:27,105
Because it's near the septic tanks,
so it's cheap.

281
00:20:27,105 --> 00:20:29,563
Mom, how did you know
about that thing I saw?

282
00:20:29,563 --> 00:20:31,646
We come to this place every year
because this is the place

283
00:20:31,646 --> 00:20:33,063
I met your father.

284
00:20:36,271 --> 00:20:39,563
My dad? What does my dad
have to do with this?

285
00:20:47,896 --> 00:20:50,938
A long time ago, I...

286
00:20:52,355 --> 00:20:55,396
met a man, here on the beach.

287
00:20:55,396 --> 00:21:01,480
He was wise and brave
and kind and... noble.

288
00:21:02,438 --> 00:21:05,855
From the moment I first saw him,
I knew that...

289
00:21:08,063 --> 00:21:12,063
that I had never met a man
like him before.

290
00:21:13,230 --> 00:21:20,063
And then I realized he was unlike
any man I had ever met before...

291
00:21:22,938 --> 00:21:28,688
because h... he wasn't a man at all.
He was a god.

292
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:38,480
You fell in love with God? Like...

293
00:21:39,771 --> 00:21:41,146
Like-- like Jesus?

294
00:21:42,355 --> 00:21:47,355
Not God. A god. Percy...

295
00:21:49,230 --> 00:21:50,313
...the stories...

296
00:21:51,313 --> 00:21:56,438
that I have told you about Greek gods
and heroes and monsters, they are real.

297
00:21:56,563 --> 00:21:58,896
- Mom--
- In those stories, I have told you

298
00:21:59,021 --> 00:22:00,730
about how gods and mortals

299
00:22:00,855 --> 00:22:02,855
- would sometimes have children together...
- Mom, please, stop.

300
00:22:02,855 --> 00:22:04,063
- ...children called demigods...
- Mom!

301
00:22:04,063 --> 00:22:07,105
...and sometimes they are known
as half-bloods.

302
00:22:09,896 --> 00:22:13,271
That's what the monster called me.
Mom, what's happening?

303
00:22:13,271 --> 00:22:14,730
You are a half-blood.

304
00:22:16,813 --> 00:22:20,021
And half-bloods are not safe in the world.

305
00:22:21,521 --> 00:22:24,813
Once they reach a certain age
and they begin...

306
00:22:26,230 --> 00:22:31,480
to understand what they are,
terrible forces are drawn to them,

307
00:22:31,605 --> 00:22:35,396
driven to harm them before they can become
strong enough to fight back.

308
00:22:35,813 --> 00:22:39,646
That is what you have been feeling.

309
00:22:39,980 --> 00:22:43,730
It has always been a part of who you are,
it was always coming, I just--

310
00:22:43,855 --> 00:22:45,021
Why are you telling me this?

311
00:22:45,021 --> 00:22:47,813
Percy, I know that this
is hard to understand,

312
00:22:47,813 --> 00:22:49,771
but you have to believe me
that this is real.

313
00:22:49,771 --> 00:22:55,980
No, this is crazy. Okay? I am not a god.
There is something wrong with my brain.

314
00:22:56,105 --> 00:22:59,396
I understand that I'm weird,
believe me, I get it,

315
00:22:59,813 --> 00:23:02,188
but I'm afraid something
may be really broken now.

316
00:23:02,188 --> 00:23:04,980
- Oh, baby, no--
- And-- and now you're telling me stories,

317
00:23:05,105 --> 00:23:06,855
like it's gonna make it okay?

318
00:23:07,063 --> 00:23:10,271
Well, I'm not a baby!
I know there's no such thing as monsters,

319
00:23:10,271 --> 00:23:13,688
I know there's no such thing as gods,
and I know for certain

320
00:23:13,938 --> 00:23:16,605
that there is no such things as demigods.

321
00:23:16,730 --> 00:23:18,605
- Who's there?

322
00:23:19,438 --> 00:23:21,521
- Mrs. Jackson? It's Grover.
- Grover?

323
00:23:21,521 --> 00:23:24,396
This is a little time sensitive.
Could someone maybe open the door?

324
00:23:24,396 --> 00:23:27,813
What is he doing here?
I don't wanna see him. Wait, Mom--

325
00:23:28,563 --> 00:23:30,896
I asked to have the night, you said
we could all leave in the morning.

326
00:23:31,021 --> 00:23:32,980
Sorry, I'm early,
but I didn't have any choice.

327
00:23:33,438 --> 00:23:35,521
Things have changed,
this is all developing a lot faster

328
00:23:35,646 --> 00:23:37,396
- than we anticipated.
- Early?

329
00:23:38,396 --> 00:23:41,021
You should have asked me before you--
Whatever it is you're gonna say,

330
00:23:41,021 --> 00:23:43,146
I don't wanna... hear it. Grover?

331
00:23:43,396 --> 00:23:44,396
Percy.

332
00:23:44,646 --> 00:23:46,605
- Okay, so something's coming...
-  Grover.

333
00:23:46,605 --> 00:23:48,271
- ...and I know that sounds really bad...
- Grover?

334
00:23:48,271 --> 00:23:49,730
...but the important thing
is not to panic.

335
00:23:49,896 --> 00:23:50,938
I'm not panicking.

336
00:23:51,063 --> 00:23:53,688
- Grover!
- Great! I'm also definitely not panicking.

337
00:23:53,688 --> 00:23:55,438
I feel very good about
how we're doing so far--

338
00:23:55,438 --> 00:23:56,771
- Grover!
- What?

339
00:23:57,063 --> 00:23:59,355
Grover, why is there half a goat
in your pants?

340
00:23:59,480 --> 00:24:00,480
Oh, it's...

341
00:24:02,271 --> 00:24:05,271
Oh! Oh, boy, she didn't tell you about...

342
00:24:06,563 --> 00:24:09,105
- You didn't tell him about me?
- You're early.

343
00:24:13,188 --> 00:24:14,855
So the important thing is not to panic.

344
00:24:15,313 --> 00:24:17,438
We'll continue this in the car.
Let's go.

345
00:24:24,480 --> 00:24:27,105
My job has been to guide you
to this moment.

346
00:24:27,438 --> 00:24:29,980
It's always an emotional rollercoaster
for a young demigod,

347
00:24:30,105 --> 00:24:32,605
- so providing a support system is really--
- Who are you?

348
00:24:33,896 --> 00:24:37,521
- I'm Grover. I'm your best friend and--
- What are you?

349
00:24:40,980 --> 00:24:45,980
- I'm a satyr. And I'm your Protector.
- You're my Protector?

350
00:24:46,438 --> 00:24:48,063
If I hadn't gotten you
kicked out of school,

351
00:24:48,063 --> 00:24:49,646
you'd have never survived the night.

352
00:24:49,855 --> 00:24:52,230
And what's chasing us now
would have found you there easily.

353
00:24:56,230 --> 00:24:57,230
I'm sorry.

354
00:24:59,063 --> 00:25:02,105
Usually, I can sense danger coming
a mile away, but this time...

355
00:25:02,771 --> 00:25:04,396
Well, none of us saw Dodds coming.

356
00:25:06,230 --> 00:25:07,230
So you knew.

357
00:25:08,063 --> 00:25:10,896
That thing that Dodds turned into,
you saw it happen?

358
00:25:11,521 --> 00:25:13,688
- Why didn't you say anything?
- I saw some of it.

359
00:25:14,563 --> 00:25:17,605
The Mist kept her hidden even from us
until it was too late.

360
00:25:17,771 --> 00:25:19,521
Mist? What's a mist?

361
00:25:20,355 --> 00:25:24,646
The Mist. It's the veil that hides
the magical world from the human world.

362
00:25:24,855 --> 00:25:28,980
My legs. Dodds' wings.
Even Dodds' absence,

363
00:25:29,271 --> 00:25:32,605
but it isn't supposed to hide things
from me. That never happens.

364
00:25:32,896 --> 00:25:34,396
Something powerful is at work here.

365
00:25:34,605 --> 00:25:36,771
The sooner we get you to camp,
the better off you're...

366
00:25:38,146 --> 00:25:41,521
- You told him about camp, right?
- Not yet, no.

367
00:25:42,146 --> 00:25:44,980
Camp is a sanctuary
for half-bloods.

368
00:25:44,980 --> 00:25:46,480
A safe space where you can learn

369
00:25:46,480 --> 00:25:49,313
who you are and what the world is like
on the other side of the Mist.

370
00:25:49,605 --> 00:25:52,105
Uh, it's not far, actually,
just a little ways past the bend up there.

371
00:25:53,230 --> 00:25:55,146
Mom, what else haven't we talked about?

372
00:25:57,438 --> 00:25:58,813
What else haven't you told me?

373
00:26:03,813 --> 00:26:04,855
Is that the Minotaur?

374
00:26:05,230 --> 00:26:08,980
Once the attacks start, they never let up.
Okay? Dodds was just the beginning.

375
00:26:09,271 --> 00:26:11,938
He is next. He-- he is brutal.
He is relentless.

376
00:26:11,938 --> 00:26:13,688
He is still wearing underpants.

377
00:26:18,355 --> 00:26:20,355
The Mythomagic cards were training.

378
00:26:20,480 --> 00:26:22,646
Everything has been training
for what's still ahead of you.

379
00:26:22,646 --> 00:26:23,980
What's ahead of me?

380
00:26:23,980 --> 00:26:25,271
-  Boys.
- Yeah?

381
00:26:25,396 --> 00:26:27,563
-  I'm actually 24.
- Hold on, please.

382
00:27:46,313 --> 00:27:47,605
Is everyone okay?

383
00:27:47,813 --> 00:27:51,063
-  Yeah, I'm okay.
-  Okay.

384
00:27:56,146 --> 00:27:57,146
This way!

385
00:28:09,146 --> 00:28:14,146
We're here. That's the boundary.
No monsters can cross it.

386
00:28:15,730 --> 00:28:17,563
Percy will be safe on the other side.

387
00:28:18,646 --> 00:28:21,480
"Percy will be..."
But won't all of us be safe?

388
00:28:26,313 --> 00:28:32,146
Grover, I am entrusting you
to protect my son, my only child.

389
00:28:32,146 --> 00:28:35,605
Don't worry, Mrs. Jackson,
Percy will be totally safe at camp--

390
00:28:35,605 --> 00:28:36,688
Swear it.

391
00:28:37,771 --> 00:28:40,355
- What's happening?
- Swear it, Grover!

392
00:28:40,813 --> 00:28:43,313
Keep him safe from anyone
or anything that comes for him,

393
00:28:43,313 --> 00:28:46,771
that wants to do harm,
that looks at him the wrong way.

394
00:28:46,771 --> 00:28:49,313
- Do you understand me?
- I swear!

395
00:29:00,688 --> 00:29:04,105
- I gotta go now, sweetheart.
- Go? What do you mean go?

396
00:29:04,105 --> 00:29:05,605
I can't go with you.

397
00:29:06,688 --> 00:29:09,313
- Why can't you?
-  She's human.

398
00:29:16,021 --> 00:29:17,563
You're gonna need to be brave now.

399
00:29:18,730 --> 00:29:22,188
Remember what I taught you.
Remember the stories I told you.

400
00:29:22,188 --> 00:29:23,938
- Especially the stories, they will tell...
- No.

401
00:29:23,938 --> 00:29:25,980
-  ...you everything...
- No way! Mom, I'm not leaving you!

402
00:29:25,980 --> 00:29:28,063
Perseus! Listen to me.

403
00:29:29,771 --> 00:29:30,771
You...

404
00:29:31,980 --> 00:29:33,980
are not broken.

405
00:29:36,188 --> 00:29:37,605
You are singular.

406
00:29:39,438 --> 00:29:40,730
You're a miracle.

407
00:29:43,146 --> 00:29:44,605
And you are my son.

408
00:29:48,938 --> 00:29:50,438
Hold fast.

409
00:29:52,688 --> 00:29:54,105
Brave the storm.

410
00:29:57,063 --> 00:29:58,146
I love you.

411
00:30:04,313 --> 00:30:06,063
- We need to move.

412
00:30:06,063 --> 00:30:08,855
- Give me your coat.
- Why? What are you gonna do?

413
00:30:08,980 --> 00:30:11,063
He smells half-blood,
that's what he's tracking, yeah?

414
00:30:11,480 --> 00:30:13,230
- That's right.
- So if he smells you

415
00:30:13,355 --> 00:30:15,063
in two directions at once,
maybe I can confuse him,

416
00:30:15,188 --> 00:30:16,730
buy us both a little time to get away.

417
00:30:16,855 --> 00:30:18,563
- Mom, please, don't--
-  Hey!

418
00:30:19,813 --> 00:30:20,980
It'll be okay.

419
00:30:41,563 --> 00:30:43,688
Go! Now!

420
00:31:01,105 --> 00:31:03,146
- Hey! Look!

421
00:31:06,146 --> 00:31:08,146
Come on. Come on.

422
00:31:15,771 --> 00:31:18,771
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no--

423
00:31:21,355 --> 00:31:22,563
- Mom!

424
00:31:24,271 --> 00:31:27,396
- Mom!

425
00:31:52,480 --> 00:31:56,855
- Per-- Percy! Percy, no!

426
00:33:15,105 --> 00:33:17,146
-  Is he okay?

427
00:33:17,355 --> 00:33:19,063
-  Alone?
-  How is that possible?

428
00:33:19,063 --> 00:33:20,646
-  Yeah.
-  Yeah, he's okay.

429
00:33:20,771 --> 00:33:22,021
He must be the one.

430
00:33:22,813 --> 00:33:24,188
Hush, Annabeth.

431
00:33:25,313 --> 00:33:29,063
He's waking. Everyone,
give him some space, please.

432
00:33:31,188 --> 00:33:34,063
Welcome to camp, Percy Jackson.

433
00:33:35,730 --> 00:33:37,355
We've been expecting you.

434
00:35:27,480 --> 00:35:29,230
Let the games begin!

435
00:35:34,980 --> 00:35:37,480
<i>It was so important I get here
'cause my father's a god.</i>

436
00:35:38,438 --> 00:35:39,730
<i>So, I'm gonna go find him.</i>

